Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 03:57:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 0/2] Bluetooth: MGMT: stop and account mesh transmissions correctly

A mesh packet is advertised through a dedicated advertising instance
(le_num_of_adv_sets + 1). Since the list_empty() check was added to
mesh_send_done_sync(), that instance is what keeps hdev->adv_instances
non-empty, so a mesh transmission never disables advertising when its
count is done or when it is cancelled: on the legacy path the packet
stays on air and the instance stays scheduled for 1000 s, with extended
advertising the set stays enabled for the duration the controller was
given. The tools/mesh-tester cases "Mesh - Send cancel - 1/2" encode the
original behaviour (the end of advertising after the cancel) and time
out on current kernels.

Independently, mesh_send_done_sync() completes the head of the pending
queue rather than the transmission that was on air, so after cancelling
the in-flight handle the next, still unsent, packet is reported complete
without having been sent.

Patch 1 tears the mesh instance down through hci_remove_advertising_sync()
on both advertising paths - that set only with extended advertising, so
other advertisers keep running - and keeps Advertising Removed from
being emitted for the internal instance. Patch 2 completes the mesh_tx
that owns the instance.

Tested with tools/test-runner (qemu) on the bluetooth tree and on
bluetooth-next, with tools/mesh-tester extended by the BlueZ patch
"tools/mesh-tester: Add extended advertising and send sequence tests"
(BREDRLE50 variants of the Send/cancel cases, and sequences that check
the handles of Mesh Packet Complete, how often the mesh set is started
and torn down, that no Advertising Removed is sent for the mesh instance,
and what Read Advertising Features lists afterwards):

  mesh-tester, 23 cases, KVM:           unpatched 10/23, patched 23/23
  mesh-tester, TCG + valgrind, 18 cases: unpatched  5/18, patched 18/18
  the 10 cancel cases, 5 repeated runs:  patched 50/50
  mgmt-tester, 501 cases, patched:      501/501

Unpatched, the cancel cases time out waiting for the end of advertising
(legacy: no LE Set Advertising Enable 0x00; extended: no LE Remove
Advertising Set) and the sequence cases report the tear-down counts off
by one or two; with the series the mesh set is disabled and removed
75 ms after each transmission on both paths and an ordinary advertising
instance alongside it is left untouched.

Iaroslav Voitovych (2):
  Bluetooth: MGMT: remove the mesh advertising instance when done
  Bluetooth: MGMT: complete the mesh transmission that was on air

